                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keeping trailers on the road starts long before something breaks. A reliable trailer preventive maintenance checklist helps reduce costly downtime, improve safety, and extend the life of your equipment. Whether you manage an entire fleet or operate a handful of trailers, preventive maintenance isn't just another item on your to-do list. It's one of the smartest investments you can make.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While daily walkarounds are important, a complete inspection requires experienced technicians who know what to look for. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, our service team helps fleets stay ahead of unexpected repairs with professional inspections, maintenance, and repairs designed to keep your equipment moving.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/trailer-preventive-maintenance-checklist-for-fleets/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Hyundai Translead dry van trailer paired with an International day cab at Sun State"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Preventive Trailer Maintenance Matters",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every mile your trailer travels puts stress on critical components. Brakes wear down, tires lose tread, suspension parts experience fatigue, and electrical connections become exposed to dirt, moisture, and vibration.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "According to the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration, proper inspection, repair, and maintenance are essential for operating commercial vehicles safely. A well-maintained trailer not only helps reduce the risk of roadside breakdowns but can also help fleets avoid costly violations during inspections.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Routine maintenance also helps you:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-matters-4",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Reduce unexpected downtime"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Improve driver safety"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Extend trailer lifespan"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Protect valuable cargo"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lower long-term repair costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stay prepared for DOT inspections"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A preventive maintenance program allows small issues to be identified before they become major repairs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
